body:
The week-start dropdown in the Uber add form was built using `"monday last week -{$i} weeks"`, which always anchors to the *previous* week's Monday. This excluded the current week entirely when logging on Sunday — the last day of the Mon–Sun work period.

## Change

**`modules/Uber/add.php`** — replaced the Monday generation logic:

```php
// Before: always starts from last week's Monday
for ($i = 0; $i < 8; $i++) {
    $monday = clone $today;
    $monday->modify("monday last week -{$i} weeks");
    $mondays[] = $monday->format('Y-m-d');
}

// After: anchors to the current week's Monday (works Mon–Sun)
$dayOfWeek = (int) $today->format('N'); // 1 = Monday, 7 = Sunday
$currentMonday = clone $today;
$currentMonday->modify('-' . ($dayOfWeek - 1) . ' days');
$currentMonday->setTime(0, 0, 0);
for ($i = 0; $i < 8; $i++) {
    $monday = clone $currentMonday;
    if ($i > 0) {
        $monday->modify("-{$i} weeks");
    }
    $mondays[] = $monday->format('Y-m-d');
}
```

The current week's Monday is now always the first (default) option regardless of which day the form is opened. The Uber period definition (Mon 00:00 → Sun 23:59) is unchanged.

